    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Choosing between a metal roof and asphalt shingles for a Utah home depends on your budget, how long you plan to stay in the house, and how the local climate (heavy winter snow, intense UV rays, and high winds) affects your property.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "depends on your budget, how long you plan to stay in the house, and how the local climate (heavy winter snow, intense UV rays, and high winds) affects your property"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Comparison Overview"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Metal Roof Pros and Cons in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Pros:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Snow Shedding: Utah winters bring heavy mountain and valley snow; metal\u2019s slick surface lets snow slide off easily rather than piling up and causing structural strain or ice dams."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Longevity: A standing-seam metal roof can last 40 to 70 years, often outliving the homeowner."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Fire & Wind Resistance: Non-combustible (great for wildfire-prone canyon or rural areas) and engineered to withstand severe wind storms."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Energy Savings: Coated metal reflects solar radiation effectively in the hot summer months.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  0,
                  1,
                  2,
                  3
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cons:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "High Upfront Investment: Costs significantly more initially\u2014often 2 to 3 times the price of traditional asphalt."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Repairs: If a metal panel gets damaged by a falling tree branch or severe hail dent, replacing it requires a specialist."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Noise Concerns: Though proper decking and insulation mute the sound, heavy rain or hail can still be louder than on shingle roofs if uninsulated.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  2,
                  4,
                  5
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Asphalt Shingle Pros and Cons in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Pros:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Lower Initial Cost: Much cheaper to buy and install upfront, making it the most common choice for budget-conscious homeowners."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Easy Repairs: Individual damaged or wind-lifted shingles can be swapped out quickly and inexpensively by a local contractor."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Versatile Aesthetics: Available in a wide array of colors and architectural styles that blend smoothly with traditional Utah suburban neighborhoods.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  4,
                  6,
                  7
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              6,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cons:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Shorter Lifespan: Intense UV exposure, high summer heat, and harsh freeze-thaw cycles degrade asphalt over 20 to 30 years (or less for basic 3-tab shingles)."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Ice Dams and Snow Retention: Asphalt holds onto snow and moisture longer, increasing the likelihood of winter ice dams along the eaves.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  1,
                  3
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Which Should You Choose?"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Choose Asphalt Shingles if you want a lower initial price tag, prefer a classic residential look, or plan to move within the next 10 to 15 years. Look into local providers like Blackridge Roofing or S&S Roofing, Inc. for shingle estimates.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Blackridge Roofing",
                "link": "https://request.angi.com/service-request-pro-direct/task/40133?spIds=134606427&businessTypes=LEADS&m=cammggeminia&entry_point_id=44949565"
              },
              {
                "text": "S&S Roofing, Inc.",
                "link": "https://request.angi.com/service-request-pro-direct/task/60419?spIds=5216259&businessTypes=LEADS&m=cammggeminia&entry_point_id=44949565"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Choose Metal Roofing if you are building or staying in your \"forever home,\" live in a heavy-snow or high-wind area, or want a long-term, low-maintenance shield against Utah\u2019s climate. You can consult local specialists like C Buxton Exteriors LLC for a metal evaluation.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3,
              5,
              8
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you share your roof's square footage and city/elevation in Utah, I can give you a rough cost and snow-load recommendation for your specific area."
      }
    ],
